{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000112",
  "title": "Maze Generator",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[dependencies]\nplotters = \"0.3\"\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "shared_source": "// \u2500\u2500 Wall Bitmask Constants \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n// Each cell stores a bitmask of REMOVED walls (carved passages).\n\npub const N: u8 = 1;\npub const E: u8 = 2;\npub const S: u8 = 4;\npub const W: u8 = 8;\n\npub const MAZE_W: usize = 25;\npub const MAZE_H: usize = 25;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Deterministic PRNG (xorshift64) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\npub struct Rng(pub u64);\n\nimpl Rng {\n    pub fn next_u64(&mut self) -> u64 {\n        self.0 ^= self.0 << 13;\n        self.0 ^= self.0 >> 7;\n        self.0 ^= self.0 << 17;\n        self.0\n    }\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Maze Generation (Recursive Backtracker) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\npub fn generate_maze(seed: u64) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let w = MAZE_W;\n    let h = MAZE_H;\n    let mut rng = Rng(seed);\n\n    // Grid where each cell stores a bitmask of carved passages\n    let mut grid = vec![0u8; w * h];\n    let mut visited = vec![false; w * h];\n    let mut stack: Vec<usize> = Vec::new();\n\n    // Start from top-left corner\n    visited[0] = true;\n    stack.push(0);\n\n    while let Some(&current) = stack.last() {\n        let cx = current % w;\n        let cy = current / w;\n\n        // Collect unvisited neighbors: (neighbor_idx, wall_from_current, wall_from_neighbor)\n        let mut neighbors: Vec<(usize, u8, u8)> = Vec::new();\n        if cy > 0 && !visited[current - w] {\n            neighbors.push((current - w, N, S));\n        }\n        if cx < w - 1 && !visited[current + 1] {\n            neighbors.push((current + 1, E, W));\n        }\n        if cy < h - 1 && !visited[current + w] {\n            neighbors.push((current + w, S, N));\n        }\n        if cx > 0 && !visited[current - 1] {\n            neighbors.push((current - 1, W, E));\n        }\n\n        if neighbors.is_empty() {\n            // Dead end \u2014 backtrack\n            stack.pop();\n        } else {\n            // Pick a random unvisited neighbor\n            let idx = (rng.next_u64() as usize) % neighbors.len();\n            let (next, wall_from, wall_to) = neighbors[idx];\n\n            // Carve passage between current and next\n            grid[current] |= wall_from;\n            grid[next] |= wall_to;\n\n            visited[next] = true;\n            stack.push(next);\n        }\n    }\n\n    grid\n}\n",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# Maze Generator \ud83c\udff0\n\n**Maze generation** algorithms create perfect mazes \u2014 mazes where every cell is reachable from every other cell, with exactly one path between any two points.\n\n## Recursive Backtracker Algorithm\n\nThe **recursive backtracker** (a depth-first search variant) is one of the most popular maze generators:\n\n1. Start at a cell, mark it **visited**\n2. While the stack is not empty:\n   - Look at the **current cell's unvisited neighbors**\n   - If there are unvisited neighbors: pick one at **random**, carve a passage to it, push it onto the stack\n   - If there are none: **backtrack** (pop the stack)\n\nThis produces mazes with long, winding corridors and relatively few dead ends \u2014 characteristic of DFS-based generators.\n\n## Representation\n\nEach cell stores a **bitmask** of carved walls: `N=1, E=2, S=4, W=8`. If a bit is set, the wall in that direction has been removed (there's a passage).",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Generate Maze",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Generate a 25\u00d725 maze using the recursive backtracker algorithm.\nlet grid = shared::generate_maze(12345);\n\nCellOutput::text(format!(\n    \"Generated {}\u00d7{} maze ({} cells, {} bytes of wall data)\",\n    shared::MAZE_W,\n    shared::MAZE_H,\n    grid.len(),\n    grid.len(),\n))\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_1\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Render Maze",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Generate and render the maze as an SVG with dark theme.\nlet grid = shared::generate_maze(12345);\nlet (w, h) = (shared::MAZE_W, shared::MAZE_H);\nlet cs = 20; // cell size in pixels\nlet img_w = (w * cs + 2) as u32;\nlet img_h = (h * cs + 2) as u32;\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (img_w, img_h)).into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&RGBColor(18, 18, 28)).unwrap();\n\n    let wall_style = ShapeStyle {\n        color: RGBColor(180, 190, 210).to_rgba(),\n        filled: false,\n        stroke_width: 2,\n    };\n\n    // Draw walls: if a wall bit is NOT set, draw that wall edge\n    for cy in 0..h {\n        for cx in 0..w {\n            let walls = grid[cy * w + cx];\n            let x0 = (cx * cs + 1) as i32;\n            let y0 = (cy * cs + 1) as i32;\n            let x1 = x0 + cs as i32;\n            let y1 = y0 + cs as i32;\n\n            if walls & shared::N == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x0, y0), (x1, y0)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n            if walls & shared::E == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x1, y0), (x1, y1)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n            if walls & shared::S == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x0, y1), (x1, y1)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n            if walls & shared::W == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x0, y0), (x0, y1)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Mark entrance (top-left) and exit (bottom-right)\n    let half = cs as i32 / 2;\n    root.draw(&Circle::new(\n        (1 + half, 1 + half),\n        5,\n        RGBColor(80, 220, 120).filled(),\n    ))\n    .unwrap();\n    root.draw(&Circle::new(\n        (\n            1 + (w - 1) as i32 * cs as i32 + half,\n            1 + (h - 1) as i32 * cs as i32 + half,\n        ),\n        5,\n        RGBColor(220, 80, 80).filled(),\n    ))\n    .unwrap();\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nSvg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_2\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_3",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Solve & Render",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use plotters::prelude::*;\n\n// Generate the same maze, solve it with BFS, and render the solution path.\nlet grid = shared::generate_maze(12345);\nlet (w, h) = (shared::MAZE_W, shared::MAZE_H);\n\n// \u2500\u2500 BFS from entrance (0,0) to exit (w-1, h-1) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nlet start = 0_usize;\nlet goal = w * h - 1;\n\nlet mut parent = vec![usize::MAX; w * h];\nlet mut visited = vec![false; w * h];\nlet mut queue = std::collections::VecDeque::new();\n\nvisited[start] = true;\nqueue.push_back(start);\n\nwhile let Some(current) = queue.pop_front() {\n    if current == goal {\n        break;\n    }\n\n    let cx = current % w;\n    let cy = current / w;\n    let walls = grid[current];\n\n    // Explore passable neighbors (wall bit set = passage exists)\n    let neighbors = [\n        (walls & shared::N != 0 && cy > 0, current.wrapping_sub(w)),\n        (walls & shared::E != 0 && cx < w - 1, current + 1),\n        (walls & shared::S != 0 && cy < h - 1, current + w),\n        (walls & shared::W != 0 && cx > 0, current.wrapping_sub(1)),\n    ];\n\n    for (passable, next) in neighbors {\n        if passable && !visited[next] {\n            visited[next] = true;\n            parent[next] = current;\n            queue.push_back(next);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Reconstruct the solution path\nlet mut path = Vec::new();\nlet mut cur = goal;\nwhile cur != usize::MAX {\n    path.push(cur);\n    cur = parent[cur];\n}\npath.reverse();\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Render maze with solution overlay \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nlet cs = 20;\nlet img_w = (w * cs + 2) as u32;\nlet img_h = (h * cs + 2) as u32;\n\nlet mut svg_buf = String::new();\n{\n    let root = SVGBackend::with_string(&mut svg_buf, (img_w, img_h)).into_drawing_area();\n    root.fill(&RGBColor(18, 18, 28)).unwrap();\n\n    let half = cs as i32 / 2;\n    let path_style = ShapeStyle {\n        color: RGBColor(0, 220, 180).to_rgba(),\n        filled: false,\n        stroke_width: 4,\n    };\n\n    // Draw solution path as connected line segments\n    for window in path.windows(2) {\n        let (ax, ay) = (window[0] % w, window[0] / w);\n        let (bx, by) = (window[1] % w, window[1] / w);\n        let p1 = (1 + ax as i32 * cs as i32 + half, 1 + ay as i32 * cs as i32 + half);\n        let p2 = (1 + bx as i32 * cs as i32 + half, 1 + by as i32 * cs as i32 + half);\n        root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![p1, p2], path_style)).unwrap();\n    }\n\n    // Draw solution dots\n    for &cell_idx in &path {\n        let cx = cell_idx % w;\n        let cy = cell_idx / w;\n        root.draw(&Circle::new(\n            (1 + cx as i32 * cs as i32 + half, 1 + cy as i32 * cs as i32 + half),\n            3,\n            RGBColor(0, 220, 180).filled(),\n        ))\n        .unwrap();\n    }\n\n    // Draw walls on top\n    let wall_style = ShapeStyle {\n        color: RGBColor(120, 130, 150).to_rgba(),\n        filled: false,\n        stroke_width: 2,\n    };\n\n    for cy in 0..h {\n        for cx in 0..w {\n            let walls = grid[cy * w + cx];\n            let x0 = (cx * cs + 1) as i32;\n            let y0 = (cy * cs + 1) as i32;\n            let x1 = x0 + cs as i32;\n            let y1 = y0 + cs as i32;\n\n            if walls & shared::N == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x0, y0), (x1, y0)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n            if walls & shared::E == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x1, y0), (x1, y1)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n            if walls & shared::S == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x0, y1), (x1, y1)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n            if walls & shared::W == 0 {\n                root.draw(&PathElement::new(vec![(x0, y0), (x0, y1)], wall_style))\n                    .unwrap();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Mark start and goal\n    root.draw(&Circle::new(\n        (1 + half, 1 + half),\n        5,\n        RGBColor(80, 220, 120).filled(),\n    ))\n    .unwrap();\n    root.draw(&Circle::new(\n        (\n            1 + (w - 1) as i32 * cs as i32 + half,\n            1 + (h - 1) as i32 * cs as i32 + half,\n        ),\n        5,\n        RGBColor(220, 80, 80).filled(),\n    ))\n    .unwrap();\n\n    root.present().unwrap();\n}\n\nCellOutput::text(format!(\"Solution path: {} steps\", path.len())).with_svg(svg_buf)\n",
      "cargo_toml": "[package]\nname = \"cell_3\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n\n[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_4",
      "order": 4,
      "label": "Algorithm Details",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## The Algorithm in Depth\n\n### Why Recursive Backtracker?\n\nThe recursive backtracker creates mazes with **long, winding corridors** because it carves as deep as possible before backtracking. This produces:\n- Few short dead ends\n- Long paths that feel satisfying to navigate\n- A \"river-like\" structure\n\n### Other Maze Algorithms\n\n| Algorithm | Character | Complexity |\n|-----------|-----------|------------|\n| **Recursive Backtracker** | Long corridors, few dead ends | O(n) time, O(n) stack |\n| **Kruskal's** | Many short dead ends, uniform feel | O(n log n) |\n| **Prim's** | Branching, tree-like structure | O(n log n) |\n| **Aldous-Broder** | Perfectly uniform | O(n\u00b2) expected |\n| **Wilson's** | Perfectly uniform | O(n\u00b2) worst case |\n\n### The BFS Solver\n\nBreadth-first search finds the **shortest path** in an unweighted graph. It explores all cells at distance 1 before distance 2, ensuring the first path found to the goal is optimal.\n\nFor weighted mazes (where passages have different costs), you'd use **Dijkstra's** or **A\\*** instead.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ]
}
